{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n\nThe user invoked Phase 3A test-body translation for `cleartext_aead_test`. The task is to translate 8 C test entries from `picoquictest/cleartext_aead_test.c` into Rust `#[test]` bodies in `rs/fq/src/tests/cleartext_aead.rs`. Key rules:\n- Tests don't need to *pass* (Phase 4 fills in API bodies); they just need to *compile*\n- No `todo!()` in test bodies unless the C body itself is `#if 0`\n- Add `todo!()` stubs to source files (`rs/fq/src/`) when the test calls non-existent API methods\n- Build gate: `cargo fmt && cargo test --no-run && cargo clippy --tests --all-features -- -D warnings`\n- No `unsafe`, no edits outside `rs/fq/src/tests/` and `rs/fq/src/` (for stubs only)\n\nTests to translate:\n- `#[test] fn clear_text_aead()` ← C `cleartext_aead_test`\n- `#[test] fn pn_ctr()` ← C `pn_ctr_test`\n- `#[test] fn cleartext_pn_enc()` ← C `cleartext_pn_enc_test`\n- `#[test] fn retry_protection_vector()` ← C `retry_protection_vector_test`\n- `#[test] fn retry_protection_v2()` ← C `retry_protection_v2_test`\n- `#[test] fn draft17_vector()` ← C `draft17_vector_test`\n- `#[test] fn pn_vector()` ← C `cleartext_pn_vector_test`\n- `#[test] fn key_rotation_vector()` ← C `key_rotation_vector_test`\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n- Phase 3A of C→Rust translation (test body translation, not implementation)\n- `PacketKey` trait (`encrypt(packet: u64, header: &[u8], payload: &mut Vec<u8>)` and `decrypt(...)`) replaces C's `picoquic_aead_encrypt_generic` / `picoquic_aead_decrypt_generic`\n- `HeaderKey` trait (`mask(sample: [u8; 16]) -> [u8; 16]`) replaces C's `ptls_cipher_init` + `ptls_cipher_encrypt` (AES-128-ECB/CTR)\n- `CryptoContext` struct (pub fields `aead_encrypt`, `aead_decrypt`, `pn_enc`, `pn_dec` as `Option<Box<dyn PacketKey/HeaderKey>>`)\n- `Connection.crypto_context: [CryptoContext; NUMBER_OF_EPOCHS]` is a `pub` field accessible from tests inside the crate\n- QUIC version enum `Version` with `#[repr(u32)]`, `Version::V1`, `Version::V2`, `INTEROP_VERSION_LATEST = Version::NineteenthInterop`\n- `VersionParameters` struct with `version_aead_key`, `version_retry_key`, `tls_prefix_label`\n- HKDF label expansion via `hkdf_expand_label` (new stub)\n- Raw AES-128-CTR cipher access via `test_pn_enc_from_raw_key` (new stub)\n- `rotate_app_secret(&mut dyn DynDigest, &mut [u8], label)` for key rotation\n- `hash_create(algorithm_name) -> Option<Box<dyn DynDigest>>` for SHA-256/SHA-384\n- `Quic::first_connection()` for getting a connection reference back after a borrow ends\n- `ConnectionId` is `#[derive(Copy, Clone)]` — can be copied by value\n- `as_bytes_mut()` on `ConnectionId` has a real implementation (not `todo!()`)\n- `encode_retry_protection` / `verify_retry_protection` for retry integrity tags\n- `create_retry_protection_context(is_enc, key, prefix_label)` for retry AEAD context\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n- **`picoquictest/cleartext_aead_test.c`** (read-only C source):\n  - Contains 8 test functions; read in sections due to 25k token limit\n  - Key findings: `cleartext_iv_cmp` always returns 0 (comparison in `#if 0`), entire `cleartext_pn_vector_test` body is `#if 0`, `cleartext_aead_vector_test_one` effectively just checks crypto contexts are non-null\n\n- **`xlate/test_translation_guide.md`** (read-only):\n  - Provides Rust API surface, naming conventions; `setup_initial_master_secret(salt, cnx_id, secret)` takes no cipher suite; `rotate_app_secret` takes `&mut dyn DynDigest`\n\n- **`rs/fq/src/tls_api.rs`** (modified — 2 new stubs added):\n  - Added after the `pn_enc_create_for_test` function:\n  ```rust\n  /// Construct a header-protection cipher context directly from a raw\n  /// 16-byte AES-128 key (no HKDF derivation).  Used by `pn_ctr_test`\n  /// to verify the AES-128-ECB keystream against a known answer.\n  /// C: `ptls_cipher_new(aead->ctr_cipher, 1, key)`.\n  pub fn test_pn_enc_from_raw_key(\n      _key: &[u8; 16],\n  ) -> Option<Box<dyn crate::tls::HeaderKey>> {\n      todo!()\n  }\n\n  /// HKDF-Expand-Label (RFC 8446 §7.1) using the QUIC-specific label\n  /// encoding.  The output length is determined by `output.len()`.\n  /// Uses SHA-256 (the hash fixed for QUIC Initial-secret derivation).\n  /// C: `ptls_hkdf_expand_label(cipher->hash, output, output_len,\n  ///    ptls_iovec(secret), label, empty_ctx, base_label)`.\n  pub fn hkdf_expand_label(\n      _label: &str,\n      _base_label: &str,\n      _secret: &[u8],\n      _output: &mut [u8],\n  ) -> Result<(), crate::Error> {\n      todo!()\n  }\n  ```\n\n- **`rs/fq/src/tests/cleartext_aead.rs`** (fully rewritten):\n  - Complete test file with all 8 translated test bodies plus 3 private helper functions\n  - Key imports: `crate::internal::{INTEROP_VERSION_LATEST, Version, format_32}`, `crate::tls_api::{...}`, `crate::utils::format_connection_id`, `crate::{ConnectionId, Instant, Quic, MAX_PACKET_SIZE, RESET_SECRET_SIZE}`, `super::util::{TEST_ALPN, TEST_FILE_CERT_STORE, TEST_FILE_SERVER_CERT, TEST_FILE_SERVER_KEY}`\n  \n  Helper functions:\n  ```rust\n  fn init_aead_packet(dest_cnx_id: ConnectionId, pn: u32, vn: u32, ptype: u8, buf: &mut [u8], target: usize) -> usize\n  fn aead_vector_test_one(test_id: ConnectionId, test_vn: u32)\n  fn test_one_pn_enc_pair(seqnum: &[u8], pn_enc: &dyn crate::tls::HeaderKey, pn_dec: &dyn crate::tls::HeaderKey, sample: &[u8; 16])\n  ```\n  \n  Key translation decisions per test:\n  - `clear_text_aead`: Creates two Quic contexts; holds both connections simultaneously (no conflict since from different Quic instances); uses `cnx_client.initial_connection_id` (pub field) and `cnx_client.crypto_context[0].aead_encrypt.as_ref().expect(...).encrypt(seqnum as u64, header, &mut payload)`\n  - `pn_ctr`: Uses `test_pn_enc_from_raw_key(&KEY)` → `cipher.mask(IV)` → verifies keystream == EXPECTED; XOR-based variable-length tests; packet PN encryption test\n  - `cleartext_pn_enc`: Starts client, creates server, uses `test_one_pn_enc_pair` with `pn_enc`/`pn_dec` via `HeaderKey::mask`\n  - `pn_vector`: Empty body — C code is entirely `#if 0`\n  - `draft17_vector`: Calls `hkdf_expand_label` 6 times (server key/iv/hp, client key/iv/hp); conditionally checks master/client/server secrets; calls `aead_vector_test_one`\n  - `retry_protection_vector`: Two phases — (1) low-level AEAD encrypt/decrypt of empty plaintext → 16-byte tag, with negative test; (2) `encode_retry_protection`/`verify_retry_protection` with positive/bad-ODCID/draft25-vector tests\n  - `retry_protection_v2`: Uses `Version::V2.parameters()` for key and prefix label; calls `encode_retry_protection` and compares to known v2 sample\n  - `key_rotation_vector`: Iterates over 3 `(hash_name, digest_size, target)` cases; calls `hash_create` + `rotate_app_secret` for each\n\n  Important data fix: `retry_protection_test_checksum[8]` is `0xf1` not `0xa1` (caught by re-reading C source at line 1158).\n\n- **`rs/fq/src/internal.rs`** (read-only, key findings):\n  - `pub const NUMBER_OF_EPOCHS: usize = 4`\n  - `pub struct Connection { pub crypto_context: [CryptoContext; NUMBER_OF_EPOCHS], pub initial_connection_id: ConnectionId, pub proposed_version: u32, ... }`\n  - `pub const INTEROP_VERSION_LATEST: Version = Version::NineteenthInterop`\n  - `Version` enum with `#[repr(u32)]` — `V1 = 0x00000001`, `V2 = 0x6b3343cf`\n  - `VersionParameters { version_aead_key: &'static [u8], version_retry_key: &'static [u8], tls_prefix_label: &'static str, ... }`\n\n- **`rs/fq/src/lib.rs`** (read-only, key findings):\n  - `ConnectionId` is `#[derive(Debug, Copy, Clone, PartialEq, Eq, ...)]`\n  - `ConnectionId::as_bytes_mut(&mut self) -> &mut [u8]` has real implementation\n  - `Quic::first_connection(&mut self) -> Option<&mut Connection>` exists (todo!())\n  - `Connection::remote_connection_id(&self) -> ConnectionId` exists (todo!())\n  - `use crate::internal::{Connection, Path, Quic}` at line 406 — lib.rs uses internal types\n\n- **`rs/fq/src/tls.rs`** (read-only, key findings):\n  - `pub trait PacketKey: Send { fn encrypt(&self, packet: u64, header: &[u8], payload: &mut Vec<u8>); fn decrypt(&self, packet: u64, header: &[u8], payload: &mut Vec<u8>) -> Result<(), Error>; }`\n  - `pub trait HeaderKey: Send { fn mask(&self, sample: [u8; 16]) -> [u8; 16]; }`\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n- **Wrong byte in checksum**: Initially wrote `retry_protection_test_checksum[8] = 0xa1` but the C source has `0xf1`. Fixed by re-reading the C source at line 1158 and applying an `Edit` to the Rust test file.\n- **`hkdf_expand_label` missing**: The function `ptls_hkdf_expand_label` in C has no counterpart in the Rust API. Added a new `todo!()` stub to `tls_api.rs`.\n- **`test_pn_enc_from_raw_key` missing**: The C test uses raw AES-128 key for CTR cipher (not HKDF-derived). `pn_enc_create_for_test` takes a secret, not a key. Added new `todo!()` stub to `tls_api.rs`.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n- **Borrow checker for dual connections**: Both `cnx_client` and `cnx_server` can be held simultaneously since they borrow from *different* `Quic` instances (`qclient` vs `qserver`). The key insight is that Rust only prevents simultaneous mutable borrows from the *same* owner.\n- **Accessing `crypto_context` fields**: Since `Connection` (= `crate::internal::Connection`) has `pub crypto_context: [CryptoContext; NUMBER_OF_EPOCHS]` and tests are inside the same crate, these fields are directly accessible.\n- **`HeaderKey::mask` vs CTR cipher**: The C `pn_ctr_test` uses raw AES-CTR for 1/2/4/8/16-byte inputs. Since the test only uses single-block operations (IV starts fresh each time), `HeaderKey::mask(sample) -> [u8; 16]` (= AES-ECB(key, sample)) covers all cases: take the first N bytes of the mask for N-byte inputs.\n- **`cleartext_iv_cmp` always returns 0**: The real IV comparison in C is inside `#if 0`. The `aead_vector_test_one` helper therefore only checks that `crypto_context[0].aead_encrypt.is_some()` and `.aead_decrypt.is_some()`.\n- **`picoquic_retry_protection_key_25`**: This C extern maps to `Version::V1.parameters().version_retry_key` in Rust; `parameters()` is `todo!()` so the test will panic there (expected behavior).\n\n6. All user messages:\n- The initial user message was the full Phase 3A test-body translation prompt specifying exactly the 8 tests to translate, the rules (faithful/idiomatic, no todo!() in test bodies except #if 0, compile is the gate), the process (read → translate → validate), and constraints (no unsafe, only edit rs/fq/src/tests/ and add stubs to source files).\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n- Run `cargo test --no-run` to verify compilation (not yet completed)\n- Run `cargo clippy --tests --all-features -- -D warnings` to verify no warnings (not yet completed)\n- Potentially fix any compilation errors found by the above commands\n- Log the shell commands to `COMMANDS.log` (per CLAUDE.md requirement)\n\n8. Current Work:\nThe assistant had just completed:\n1. Adding two new `todo!()` stubs to `rs/fq/src/tls_api.rs`:\n   - `test_pn_enc_from_raw_key(_key: &[u8; 16]) -> Option<Box<dyn crate::tls::HeaderKey>>`\n   - `hkdf_expand_label(_label, _base_label, _secret, _output) -> Result<(), crate::Error>`\n2. Writing the complete `rs/fq/src/tests/cleartext_aead.rs` with all 8 translated test bodies plus 3 private helpers (`init_aead_packet`, `aead_vector_test_one`, `test_one_pn_enc_pair`)\n3. Fixing a data error: `retry_protection_test_checksum[8]` changed from `0xa1` to `0xf1`\n4. Running `cargo fmt` (completed successfully, modified both files)\n\nThe `cargo test --no-run` and `cargo clippy` steps had not yet been run when the summary was requested.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\nContinue with the validation steps as specified in the task:\n```\ncd rs/fq && cargo test --no-run\ncd rs/fq && cargo clippy --tests --all-features -- -